TinyEXIF began in 2013 as a fork of the easyexif library
(https://github.com/mayanklahiri/easyexif) by Mayank Lahiri, which was
released under the BSD-2-Clause license below. Portions of TinyEXIF still
derive from that code and remain additionally subject to these terms; see
LICENSE for the MIT terms covering TinyEXIF's own contributions.

The following is easyexif's license notice, reproduced verbatim as published
upstream at https://github.com/mayanklahiri/easyexif/blob/master/LICENSE
(retrieved 2026-08-22).

Note on the copyright years: the range below is upstream's own, taken from
that current LICENSE file. It has not been reconciled against the 2013 state
of easyexif that TinyEXIF forked, and upstream's own exif.h carries a
different range ("2010-2016"). It is reproduced here exactly as published
rather than adjusted, on the principle that restating someone else's
copyright notice with edited dates is worse than quoting it as it stands.
If Mayank Lahiri would prefer a different range or wording, that preference
governs and this file should be updated to match.

